# KNOWN GAP -- CHAIN-LINK class, RETURN-TYPE-ARM axis x RECEIVER-KIND axis.
#
# CELL: the outer link is `.split(",")`, a NAME-LIST arm of `infer_expr_type`'s
# builtin ladder that does NOT publish `expr_link_types[span.end]`, and the
# receiver is a USER-DEFINED (equip) method call rather than a builtin one.
#
# INTENDED OUTPUT: `3`. Rust gg answers `3` (regenerated 2026-08-29:
# `./target/debug/gg run tests/fixtures/known_gaps/chain_link_split_on_user_method_result.gg`).
#
# TODAY the SELF-HOST emits C that will not compile:
#   error: incompatible types when assigning to type 'Str' from type 'GorgetArray'
# The lowerer reads the unique `expr_link_types[span.end]` key FIRST; only 3 of
# the ladder's ~26 exits publish there (infer.gg:677 registry, :749 bool
# predicates, :771 tag check), so this arm falls back to the CONTENDED
# `expr_types[span.start]` slot every link of a postfix spine shares and mints
# the outer link's destination with its RECEIVER's type (`Str`).
#
# PRE-EXISTING, not a regression: identical on a pristine `2d619258` driver.
#
# CONTROL that establishes this is the CHAIN spelling and not `split` itself --
# both compile and run correctly on both lanes today, so they are recorded here
# rather than wired as live lines that would change the asserted output:
#   String loc = h.make()          then  print(loc.split(",").len())   -> 3
#   String s = "a,b,c"             then  print(s.split(",").len())     -> 3
#
# HEAP-FORCED: the receiver is a String field read back out of a struct, never a
# literal -- a literal receiver constant-folds and is a false negative.
#
# THE CLASS FIX IS NOT A RECEIVER GATE. This was filed under todo/t0712 on
# the claim that gating the ladder's name-list arms on the receiver type
# closed all five chain-link cells at once. R47 Track D1 BUILT the gate and
# MEASURED it: it closes ZERO — this fixture fails identically, byte for
# byte, with and without it. It cannot help, by construction: this method is
# not on the gated name list at all. What breaks the cell is that its ladder
# arm never PUBLISHES `expr_link_types[span.end]`, so `lower_types.gg`
# falls back to the CONTENDED `expr_types[span.start]` key that every link of
# a postfix spine shares. Publishing from every arm was also built and
# measured: it regressed ten `self_host_runtime` rows, because
# `infer.gg`'s `clone|copy|sorted|reversed|filter` arm answers the
# TYPECHECKER's type (`Vector[int]`) where the lowerer needs the LOWERING
# type (`FilterIter`). Reconciling those two is the real fix and it is a
# different axis from receiver typing; filed, and it starts at a scout.
# Graduate this cell and its four siblings out of known_gaps/ in the round that
# lands that fix.
struct Holder:
    String s

equip Holder:
    String make(self):
        return self.s

void main():
    Holder h = Holder("a,b,c")
    print(h.make().split(",").len())
